  "issue_number": 15282,
  "issue_title": "Vapor: components removed from v-for remain retained by the parent scope",
  "issue_body": "### Vue version\n\n3.6.0-rc.3\n\n### Link to minimal reproduction\n\nhttps://play.vuejs.org/#\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open the reproduction in Chrome.\n2. Open DevTools and select **Memory**.\n3. Select **Heap snapshot** and take a snapshot.\n4. Click **Run 100 x 1,000 mount/unmount cycles**.\n5. Wait until `Completed cycles` is `100` and `Attached children` is `0`.\n6. Click **Collect garbage** three times.\n7. Take another heap snapshot.\n8. Select **Objects retained by detached DOM nodes**, or filter for `Detached`.\n\nThe second snapshot contains detached buttons from the removed `Child` components.\n\n### What is expected?\n\nRemoving an item from `v-for` should unmount the child component and release the component instance and its DOM.\n\nRunning the same mount/unmount cycle multiple times should not increase the number of retained DOM nodes.\n\n### What is actually happening?\n\nThe child components are unmounted, but the parent scope still retains their component instances and DOM blocks.\nRetained nodes increase after every cycle and are released only when the parent app is unmounted.\n\nI also tested this in a separate Vite production build. Each sample used a new browser context and three\n`HeapProfiler.collectGarbage` calls before reading `Performance.getMetrics().Nodes`.\n\n| Mode                                   | Retained Nodes delta after cycles 1 / 2 / 3 / 4 |\n| -------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| VDOM parent + VDOM child               | `0 / 0 / 0 / 0`                                 |\n| Vapor parent + inline native element   | `2 / 2 / 2 / 2`                                 |\n| Vapor parent + Vapor child             | `2002 / 4002 / 6002 / 8002`                     |\n| VDOM parent + Vapor child with interop | `3005 / 6005 / 9005 / 12005`                    |\n\n`JSHeapUsedSize` also increases after every component cycle.\n\nThe heap snapshot contains `100002` detached child buttons after 100 pure Vapor cycles. The retaining path is:\n\n```text\n#app\n-> __vue_app__\n-> parent component instance\n-> scope\n-> cleanups[]\n-> cleanup closure\n-> removed child component instance\n-> block\n-> detached <button>\n```\n\n### System Info\n\n```shell\nSystem:\n  OS: Windows 10 10.0.19045\n  CPU: AMD Ryzen 9 5950X 16-Core Processor\nBinaries:\n  Node: 24.15.0\n  Bun: 1.3.14\nBrowsers:\n  Chromium: 151.0.7922.34\nnpmPackages:\n  vue: 3.6.0-rc.3\n  @vitejs/plugin-vue: 6.0.8\n  vite: 8.1.5\n```\n\n### Any additional comments?\n\nThe issue occurs when a `v-for` item is a child component. An inline native element does not show the same growth.\n\nIn `v3.6.0-rc.3`, the direct component path in `createFor` does not create a per-item `EffectScope`.\n`createComponent()` registers this cleanup in the active enclosing scope:\n\n```ts\nonScopeDispose(() => unmountComponent(instance));\n```\n\nRemoving the item unmounts the child, but the cleanup closure remains in the parent scope. The closure retains the\nunmounted instance and its `block` until the parent scope stops. The heap retaining path matches this ownership chain.\n\nRelevant source:\n\n- [`apiCreateFor.ts`](https://github.com/vuejs/core/blob/v3.6.0-rc.3/packages/runtime-vapor/src/apiCreateFor.ts)\n- [`component.ts`](https://github.com/vuejs/core/blob/v3.6.0-rc.3/packages/runtime-vapor/src/component.ts)\n- [`vFor.ts`](https://github.com/vuejs/core/blob/v3.6.0-rc.3/packages/compiler-vapor/src/transforms/vFor.ts)\n\nI did not find an open or closed issue with the `scope: vapor` label for this case. Issues #15234, #15236, #14773, and\n#15276 cover different lifecycle, Teleport, directive, and dynamic-slot problems.",
  "merged_at": "2026-08-13T08:33:35Z",
